# Phase task completion

When you **finish implementing** a file under `docs/phases/**/tasks/*.md` (or the user says a task is done), **close the task in the same turn** before considering the work done.

## 1. Task file — mark complete

Immediately under the `# <nn> —` title, add or update:

```markdown
> **Status:** Complete (YYYY-MM-DD). Next: [<nn+1>-….md](./….md).
```

Then in **Verify (stop gate)**, change **every** `- [ ]` to `- [x]`. Do not leave partial checklists.

## 2. Phase `STATUS.md`

Update the phase folder’s [`STATUS.md`](../../docs/phases/README.md) in the same change set:

| Section | Action |
|---------|--------|
| **Right now — do this next** | Point at the **next** task file (link + one-line deliverable). |
| **Recently completed** | Prepend a bullet for the task just finished (task id, short deliverable, date). |
| **Updated:** line | Set to today’s date. |

Follow [`01-task-index.md`](../../docs/phases/02-ui-sync/tasks/01-task-index.md#status-discipline) when present in the active phase.

## 3. Root `STATUS.md`

Update [`STATUS.md`](../../STATUS.md) **only** when the whole phase’s definition of done is met (repoint **Active phase**). Per-task progress lives in the phase `STATUS.md`.

## Do not skip

- Finishing code without updating the task verify checklist and STATUS is incomplete work.
- If verify cannot pass yet, do **not** mark the task complete; leave STATUS pointing at the current task and say what blocks the gate.
